juris placare aut lenire <NOTE N="j" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0143" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0143D"></COL> j 1  <HI REND="ITALIC">regorem</HI>  (em.  <HI REND="ITALIC">rigorem)—linire.</HI></NOTE>  specialiter exoramur <NOTE N="k" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0143" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0143D"></COL> k 1  <HI REND="ITALIC">exoratur,</HI>  em.  <HI REND="ITALIC">exoramur.</HI></NOTE> ,
id observetur, ut rescripta ante edictum propositum
impetrata suam <NOTE N="l" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0143" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0143D"></COL> l 1  <HI REND="ITALIC">sua,</HI>  em.  <HI REND="ITALIC">suam.</HI></NOTE>  habeant firmitatem, nec rescripto
posteriore derogetur priori. Quae vero postea sint
elicita, nullum robur habeant, nisi consentanea <NOTE N="m" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0143" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0143D"></COL> m 1  <HI REND="ITALIC">Consentaneas,</HI>  em.  <HI REND="ITALIC">consentanea.</HI></NOTE>  sint
legibus <NOTE N="n" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0143" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0143D"></COL> n 1  <HI REND="ITALIC">Leges,</HI>  em.  <HI REND="ITALIC">legibus.</HI></NOTE>  publicis; maxime cum inter aequitatem <NOTE N="o" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0143" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0143D"></COL> o 1  <HI REND="ITALIC">Equitate,</HI>  em.  <HI REND="ITALIC">aequitatem.</HI></NOTE> 
jusque <NOTE N="p" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0143" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0143D"></COL> p In h. V. desinit textus folii primi codicis 1; sequentia
