 <HI REND="ITALIC">Aug. V et Licinio Caes.</HI> <NOTE N="e" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155C"></COL> e Edd. ante Be. om.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Caes.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Coss.</HI>  (319).</P> <P COM="0155">INTERPR.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Si quis contra eos qui in annis minoribus
constituti sunt litem forte commoverit, aut si a parte
ipsorum reus aliquis</HI> <NOTE N="f" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155C"></COL> f 5 om.  <HI REND="ITALIC">aliquis.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">arguatur, ex eo tempora computanda
sunt, ex quo tutor sive</HI> <NOTE N="g" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155C"></COL> g Sich. in m.  <HI REND="ITALIC">vel.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">curator minoris</HI> <NOTE N="h" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155C"></COL> h Nonn. codd.  <HI REND="ITALIC">fortasse—aperte—tempore—minores.</HI></NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">aut</HI> <NOTE N="i" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155C"></COL> i Sich. Cui. 1. Aur. Lugd. om.  <HI REND="ITALIC">aut</HI>  et 20 mox  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">per judicem aut per curiam intulerit seu exceperit
actionem: ita tamen, ut si in diversis provinciis
istius officii</HI> <NOTE N="j" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155C"></COL> j Multi codd., Sich. Cui 1. Aur. Lugd.  <HI REND="ITALIC">istius modi
hom.,</HI>  sed Sich. Cui. 1 Aur. Lug. in m.  <HI REND="ITALIC">istius officii.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">homines sunt, id est, curatores vel tutores,
qui minorum causas tueantur</HI> <NOTE N="k" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155C"></COL> k  <HI REND="ITALIC">cultores—tuentur.</HI></NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">qui in eadem provincia
fuerint</HI> <NOTE N="l" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155C"></COL> l 20 cum al. codd. et Sich.  <HI REND="ITALIC">fuerit.</HI></NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ubi intentio nata probatur</HI> <NOTE N="m" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155C"></COL> m 20  <HI REND="ITALIC">proturbatur.</HI></NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ipsi aut
ingerant aut excipiant actiones: quia nolumus</HI> <NOTE N="n" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155C"></COL> n 5 volumus.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ut ad
aliam provinciam defensores minorum pro audientiae
necessitate ducantur</HI> <NOTE N="o" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155C"></COL> o Seqq. extant in codd. 5—10, 12—14, 16—19;
des. in rell. codd. et ap. Sich.</NOTE> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">Hoc de jure adjectum est.</HI></P></DIV2> <DIV2 COM="0155" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0155">DE RELATIONIBUS.</HEAD> <P COM="0155"><COL N="0155B"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Constantinus A. Profuturo Pf. annonae.</HI>  Si quis judicum
duxerit esse referendum, nihil pronuntiet <NOTE N="p" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155C"></COL> p Cod. Just.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Imp. Constantinus A.—nihil inter
partes pron.</HI></NOTE> ,
sed magis super quo <NOTE N="q" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155C"></COL> q 4, edd. ante Be. ex Cod. Just. ed.  <HI REND="ITALIC">quo.</HI></NOTE>  haesitandum putaverit, nostram
consulat scientiam, aut, si tulerit sententiam, minime
postea, ne a se provocetur, relatione promissa <NOTE N="r" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155C"></COL> r Cod. Just.  <HI REND="ITALIC">praemissa,</HI>  imp. Go., sed recte Hal.
 <COL N="0155D"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">promissa.</HI></NOTE> 
terreat litigantes <NOTE N="s" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155D"></COL> s In Cod. Just. ita pergitur:  <HI REND="ITALIC">sciens quod si hoc fecerit,
nihilominus jure appellationis res agitabitur.
Sed nec ad nos mittatur aliquid, quod plena instructione
indigeat. Quoties autem ad nostram scientiam
judex se polliceatur relaturum, consultationis exemplum
litigatoribus illico edi apud acta jubeat: ut si qui forte
relatio minus plena, vel contraria videatur, is refutatorias
preces similiter apud acta sine aliqua frustratoria
dilatione offerat.</HI>  Desumpta sunt haec, sed mutatis w.,
ex c. 1 sq. tit.</NOTE> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dat.</HI>  IV.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Id.</HI> <NOTE N="t" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155D"></COL> t Cod. Just.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Kal.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Febr. Sirmio</HI> <NOTE N="u" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155D"></COL> u Be. Cod. Just.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sirmii.</HI>  Mox Cod. Just. om. C.</NOTE> ,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Constantino A. V. et Licinio C. Coss.</HI>  (319).</P></DIV2> <DIV2 COM="0155" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0155">DE FILIIS MILITARIUM <NOTE N="v" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155D"></COL> v Cui. 1—Ri*. in indice tit.  <HI REND="ITALIC">militarium et apparitorum.</HI> 
Cod. Just.  <HI REND="ITALIC">De filiis officialium militarium,
qui in bello moriuntur.</HI>  Cum rubro h. tit. incipit folium
78, codicis.</NOTE>  APPARITORUM ET
VETERANORUM.</HEAD> <P COM="0155"><HI REND="ITALIC">Imp. Constantinus A. ad Optavianum</HI> <NOTE N="x" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155D"></COL> x Go. em.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Octavianum,</HI>  qui fuit hoc anno Corrector
 <COL N="0156C"></COL> Lucaniae et Bruttiorum. Vid c. 2 C. Th. de Episcopis
 <CITN>(XVI, 2)</CITN> .</NOTE> . Veteranorum
 <COL N="0156A"></COL> liberos aptos militiae, quorum quidam ut desides
recusant militarium munerum functionem, quidam
adeo ignavi sunt, ut cum dispendio corporis militiae
velint necessitatem evadere, jubemus, si ad militiam
inutiles resectis digitis judicentur, curialibus
sine aliqua ambiguitate muneribus atque obsequiis
aggregari.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dat.</HI>  XIV.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Kal. Mart. Sirmio</HI> <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0156" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0156C"></COL> a Ita codex, Cui. 1—Ri*. Sed Be.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sirmii.</HI></NOTE> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">Accepta</HI> 
VII.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Id. April. Regio</HI> <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0156" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0156C"></COL> b Ita codex, Cui. 1—Ri*, Sed Be.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Regii.</HI>  Mox.
Aur. Lugd. Go.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cons.</HI></NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Constantino A. V. et Licinio
C. Coss.</HI>  (319).</P></DIV2> <DIV2 COM="0156" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0156">DE BONIS VACANTIBUS.</HEAD> <P COM="0156"><HI REND="ITALIC">Constantinus A. ad Priscum Rationalem.</HI>  Ne principali
liberalitate praeventa dominium quis rei alienae affectet,
jubemus, quoties jure suadente aliquorum
bona ex officio tuo fuerint occupata, breves eorum
 <COL N="0156B"></COL> plenissimos ad virum perfectissimum comitem et <NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0156" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0156C"></COL> c I.  <HI REND="ITALIC">comet.</HI></NOTE> 
amicum nostrum mitti, ne fraudibus Caesarianorum
minuantur, vel petentibus aliquid abjuretur; poena
contra rationalem et officium ejus proposita, si petitorem
ante possidere permiserit id, quod ei donatum
est, priusquam <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0156" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0156C"></COL> d Til.—Cuj. 2*  <HI REND="ITALIC">prius, quam.</HI>  Go.—Ri.*  <HI REND="ITALIC">prius
quam.</HI></NOTE>  praedicti breves commoverint.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dat.
V. Id.</HI> <NOTE N="e" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0156" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0156C"></COL> e Fol. 87 <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0156" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0156C"></COL> b Ita codex, Cui. 1—Ri*, Sed Be.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Regii.</HI>  Mox.
Aur. Lugd. Go.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cons.</HI></NOTE>  cod. 4. Mox Be.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sirmii.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Mart. Sirmio, Constantino A. V. et Licinio
C. Coss.</HI>  (319).</P></DIV2> <DIV2 COM="0156" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0156">DE FALSA MONETA.</HEAD> <P COM="0156"><HI REND="ITALIC">Imp. Constantinus A. ad Verinum</HI> <NOTE N="f" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0156" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0156C"></COL> f Reinesius add.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Pf. U.</HI>  Go.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Vicar, Afr.</HI>  Vid. supr.
IX, 15, 1.</NOTE> . Quicumque
adulterina fecerit numismata <NOTE N="g" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0156" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0156D"></COL> g I, 4, Til.—Ri*.  <HI REND="ITALIC">nomismata.</HI> <NOTE N="n" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155C"></COL> n 5 volumus.</NOTE>  I.  <HI REND="ITALIC">vel si decur.</HI></NOTE> , poenam pro discretione
sexus et conditionis suae diversitate sustineat,
hoc est ut, si decurio vel decurionis <NOTE N="p" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155C"></COL> p Cod. Just.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Imp. Constantinus A.—nihil inter
partes pron.</HI></NOTE>  sit filius, exterminatus
genitali solo ad quamcumque in longinquo
positam civitatem sub perpetui exilii conditione mittatur,
 <COL N="0156C"></COL> ac super facultatibus <NOTE N="h" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0156" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0156D"></COL> h Til. mendose  <HI REND="ITALIC">faculatibus.</HI></NOTE>  ejus ad nostram scientiam
referatur; si plebeius, ut rebus amissis perpetuae
damnationi <NOTE N="i" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0156" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0156D"></COL> i Recte B.: «scil. in metalla, nec admittenda est
Gfr. emend.  <HI REND="ITALIC">deportationi,</HI> » quamquam confirmatur
Antiquis Summariis Codicis Theodosiani a me editis
Lipsiae 1834, 8. p. 5, ubi  <HI REND="ITALIC">si plebius, perpetuo exilio
mancipetur.</HI></NOTE>  dedatur; si servilis conditionis, ultimo
supplicio subjugetur.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dat. et</HI> <NOTE N="j" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0156" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0156D"></COL> j Ita cod. 4 et edd. ante Be. Hic tria puncta interponit
inter  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dat.</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">et,</HI>  quod non congruit cum ejus
ann.: « <HI REND="ITALIC">et</HI>  delend. videtur. Non enim dat. et acc. eodem
esse die potuit, sed dat. dies excidit.» Erat
autem hoc tempore Constantinus Sirmii in Pannonia,
Verinus Karthagine. Recte igitur a Be. lacuna indicata
est; in qua indicanda imitatus eum essem, si non
mallem codicem repraesentare. Vera scriptura videtur
latere in cod. I, qui pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Acc.</HI>  XV.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Kal</HI>  habet pp.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">id.</HI>   <CITN>(Dat. et Prop. Id. Apr.)</CITN>  Puto igitur scrib. esse
