In Cod. Just. add.  <HI REND="ITALIC">et de decimariis sublatis.</HI></NOTE> .</HEAD> <P COM="0189"><HI REND="ITALIC">Imp. Constantinus</HI> <NOTE N="h" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0189" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0189C"></COL> h Cod. Just.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Imppp. Constantinus, Constantius et
Constans AAA.,</HI>  improbb. Go. et Heineccio ad Leg.
Jul. et Pap. Popp. II, 21  <CITN>(Amstel. 1731, in-4 <SUP>o</SUP> , p. 345)</CITN> ;
sed add. Heineccius:  <HI REND="ITALIC">nisi suspicari mecum malis, filios
illud patris edictum iisdem poene verbis, ut solet
fieri, firmasse.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">A. ad Populum.</HI>  Qui jure veteri
caelibes habebantur, imminentibus legum terroribus
liberentur, atque ita vivant, ac si numero maritorum
matrimonii foedere fulcirentur, sitque omnibus
aequa conditio capessendi, quod <NOTE N="i" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0189" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0189C"></COL> i Ita Be. auct. Go. ex Cod. Just.; rell. cum. cod.
 <COL N="0189D"></COL> Lugd.  <HI REND="ITALIC">quo,</HI>  male.</NOTE>  quisque mereatur.
Nec vero quisquam orbus habeatur: proposita <NOTE N="j" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0189" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0189D"></COL> j Cod. Just.  <HI REND="ITALIC">et prop.</HI></NOTE> 
huic nomini damna non noceant. § 1. Quam
rem et circa feminas aestimamus <NOTE N="k" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0189" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0189D"></COL> k Cod. Just.  <HI REND="ITALIC">existimamus,</HI>  impr. Go.</NOTE> , earumque cervicibus
 <COL N="0189B"></COL> imposita <NOTE N="l" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0189" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0189D"></COL> l Aur. Lugd.  <HI REND="ITALIC">i Npositi,</HI>  err.</NOTE>  juris imperia, velut quaedam juga
solvimus promiscue omnibus. § 2. <NOTE N="m" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0189" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0189D"></COL> m Seqq. des. in Cod. Just.</NOTE>  Verum hujus
beneficii maritis et uxoribus inter se usurpatio non
patebit, quorum fallaces plerumque blanditiae vix
etiam opposito juris rigore <NOTE N="n" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0189" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0189D"></COL> n Go. in comm.  <HI REND="ITALIC">vigore.</HI></NOTE>  cohibentur, sed maneat
inter istas personas legum prisca auctoritas.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dat.
prid. kal. Febr. Serdica</HI> <NOTE N="o" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0189" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0189D"></COL> o Ita Go.; rell.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Serdicae.</HI>  Go. in Chron. p. XVIII.:
