 <COL N="0282C"></COL> ejxwvlhû dixovnoia× prevpei gaúr thðé hJmetevraé makariovthti hßû
ajpolauvomen suún Qewðé, toú touúû ejp1 ejlpivsin ajgaqaiðû biouðntaû,
ajpoú pavshû ajtavktou plavnhû eijû thún eujqeiðan oJdoún
ajpoú touð skovtouû ejpiú toú fwðû, ajpoú mataiovthtoû eijû thún
ajlhvqeian, ajpoú qanavtou proúû swthrivan aægesqai. uJpeúr deú
touð thðû qerapeivaû tauvthû kaiú ajnagkaivan genevsqai thún
ijscuún prosetavxamen kaqwúû proeivrhtai, uJpoú pavnta taú thðû
deisidaimonivaû uJmwðn sunevdria, pavntwn fhmiv twðn aiJretikwðn
touúû eujkthrivouû, eiæge eujkthrivouû ojnomavzein oiækouû
proshvkei, ajfaireqevntaû ajnantirjrJhvtoû, thðé kaqolikhðé 1Ekklhsivaé
cwrivû tinoúû uJperqevsewû paradoqhðnai. touúû deú
loipouúû tovpouû toiðû dhmosivoiû proskriqhðnai. kaiú mhdemivan
uJmiðn eijû toú eJxhðû touð sunagageiðn eujmavreian perileifqhðnai×
oåpwû ejkthðû ejnestwvshû, 1eegr_mhvraû, ejn mhdeniú tovpwé
mhv te dhmosivwé mhv t1 ijdiwtikwðé, taú ajqevmita uJmwðn susthvmata
 <COL N="0282D"></COL> ajqroisqhðnai tolmhvshé× proteqhvtw.</FOREIGN></P></DIV3></DIV2> <DIV2 COM="0282" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0282">DE MAGISTRATIBUS MUNICIPALIBUS.</HEAD> <COL N="0283A"></COL> <P COM="0283"><HI REND="ITALIC">Imp. Constantinus A. ad Florentinum P. P.</HI>  Decuriones
ad Magistratum, vel exactionem annonarum
ante tres menses, vel amplius nominari debent, ut,
si querimonia eorum justa videatur, sine impedimento
in absolvendi locum aliis subrogetur.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dat. Id. April.
Constantinop., Severo et Rufino Coss.</HI>  (323)  <CITN>(Ex Cod.
Just.)</CITN> .</P></DIV2></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0283" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0283">Anno Domini 324.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Crispo</HI>  III  <HI REND="ITALIC">et Constantino</HI>  III  <HI REND="ITALIC">Caess. Coss.</HI></HEAD> <DIV2 COM="0283" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0283">DE HIS QUI NUMERO LIBERORUM <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0283" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0283C"></COL> a 4  <HI REND="ITALIC">De his qui numero libero liberorum.</HI></NOTE>  VEL PAUPERTATE
EXCUSATIONEM MERUERINT <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0283" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0283C"></COL> b Cod. Just.  <HI REND="ITALIC">meruerunt.</HI></NOTE> .</HEAD> <P COM="0283"><HI REND="ITALIC">Imp. Constantinus A. Dalmatio.</HI>  Quoniam cognovimus
nonnullos vacationem a nobis personalium munerum
impetrasse, alienos pro suis liberis <NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0283" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0283C"></COL> c Go.: «Sustineri potest: malim tamen,  <HI REND="ITALIC">liberos.»</HI></NOTE>  nostris
 <COL N="0283B"></COL> conspectibus offerentes, jubemus eos, cum hoc probatum
sit <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0283" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0283C"></COL> d Go.: «Probatum fuerit.»</NOTE> , indulto beneficio privari, eos autem, qui
cujuscumque sexus liberos quinque habeant <NOTE N="e" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0283" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0283C"></COL> e 4, Til.  <HI REND="ITALIC">habeat.</HI>  Cod. Just. inc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Eos, qui c. s. l. q.
habent.</HI></NOTE> , impetrata
semel vacatione potiri <NOTE N="f" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0283" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0283C"></COL> f 4  <HI REND="ITALIC">potiris,</HI>  sed del.  <HI REND="ITALIC">s.</HI>  Cod. Just.  <HI REND="ITALIC">potiri convenit:
ita ut.</HI></NOTE> , ita ut, si in hoc numero
filius legitimae aetatis <NOTE N="g" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0283" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0283C"></COL> g Cod. Just.  <HI REND="ITALIC">aetatis legitimae filius.</HI></NOTE>  inveniatur, obeundis <NOTE N="h" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0283" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0283C"></COL> h 4  <HI REND="ITALIC">obeundi,</HI>  rubro col. add.  <HI REND="ITALIC">s.</HI></NOTE> 
statim pro suo patre muneribus applicetur <NOTE N="i" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0283" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0283C"></COL> i Apud Go. desunt  <HI REND="ITALIC">applicetur—legibus,</HI>  err. typ.</NOTE> ; patribus
qui filios vel filias quinque habuerint, promissa
legibus <NOTE N="j" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0283" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0283C"></COL> j Julia et Papia.</NOTE>  immunitate servanda. § 1. Quod si quis
propter censum tenuem <NOTE N="k" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0283" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0283C"></COL> k Cod. Just.  <HI REND="ITALIC">tenuiorem.</HI></NOTE>  vacationem meruerit, atque
hoc probaverit, beneficio potiatur, si <NOTE N="l" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0283" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0283D"></COL> l Be. cj.  <HI REND="ITALIC">nec,</HI>  ut Hal. Cuj. in c. 6 Cod. Just. cit.</NOTE>  propter rerum
angustias ad personalia vocabatur <NOTE N="m" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0283" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0283D"></COL> m Go. cj. in not.  <HI REND="ITALIC">vocabitur,</HI>  probb. Be. et Spangenb.;
Cod. Just.  <HI REND="ITALIC">vocatur,</HI>  Hal. Cuj.  <HI REND="ITALIC">vocetur.</HI>  Sed faciendum
esse duco cum Go., qui in comment. vulgatam
scripturam ita interpretatur:  <HI REND="ITALIC">«Si propter rerum
angustias</HI>  et pensandis muneribus patrimonialibus  <HI REND="ITALIC">ad
personalia hactenus vocabatur obsequia,</HI>  id est personalibus
muneribus subjectus fuit, vacatione plenissima
et  <HI REND="ITALIC">beneficio deinceps potiatur.»</HI></NOTE>  obsequia.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dat.</HI> 
