In multis codd. om.  <HI REND="ITALIC">C.</HI>  Epit. Mon.  <HI REND="ITALIC">et Const. V. C.
Coss.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et Constantio C. Coss.</HI>  (326).</P> <P COM="0313">INTERPRETATIO.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Si qua ingenua mulier servo proprio
se occulte miscuerit, capitaliter puniatur. Servus etiam,
qui in adulterio</HI> <NOTE N="r" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0313" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0313D"></COL> r Nonn. codd.  <HI REND="ITALIC">in adulterium d. conjunctus f.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">dominae convictus fuerit, ignibus
exuratur. In</HI> <NOTE N="s" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0313" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0313D"></COL> s Seqq. ap. Sich. ita scripta sunt:  <HI REND="ITALIC">In pot. habent
 <COL N="0314C"></COL> criminis accusationem servi, ut si detulerint audiantur.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">potestate habeat hujus modi crimen quicumque
 <COL N="0314A"></COL> voluerit accusare. Servi etiam aut ancillae, si de
hoc crimine accusationem detulerint, odiantur</HI> <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0314" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0314C"></COL> a Aur. Lugd. add.  <HI REND="ITALIC">quia jubet lex puniri nefarios.</HI> 
ex Aeg. summa.</NOTE> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">ea tamen
ratione, ut si probaverint, libertatem consequantur,
si</HI> <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0314" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0314C"></COL> b Ap. Ri. Ri*. add.  <HI REND="ITALIC">se.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">fefellerint, puniantur</HI> <NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0314" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0314C"></COL> c Aur. Lugd. add.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et qui ex tali conjunctione fuerint
nati, in mundina tantum maneant libertate, et a matris
haereditate in omnibus fiant extranei</HI>  ex Aeg. summa.</NOTE> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">Haereditas mulieris, quae se
tali crimine maculaverit, vel filiis</HI> <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0314" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0314C"></COL> d 20  <HI REND="ITALIC">fili</HI>  et 21  <HI REND="ITALIC">si sint.</HI></NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">si sunt ex marito
suscepti, vel propinquis ex lege venientibus tribuatur.</HI></P></DIV2> <DIV2 COM="0314" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0314">DE EPISCOPIS.</HEAD> <P COM="0314"><HI REND="ITALIC">Imp. Constantinus A. ad Ablavium Pf.P.</HI>  Neque vulgari
consensu, neque quibuslibet petentibus sub specie clericorum
a muneribus publicis vacatio deferatur, nec
temere et citra modum populi clericis connectantur <NOTE N="e" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0314" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0314C"></COL> e 4  <HI REND="ITALIC">conectantur,</HI>  rubro col. corr.  <HI REND="ITALIC">connectantur.</HI></NOTE> ,
sed cum defunctus fuerit clericus, ad vicem defuncti
alius allegetur <NOTE N="f" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0314" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0314C"></COL> f In m. Cuj. l. Cuj. 2, 2 *:  <HI REND="ITALIC">«alias eligatur»</HI>  et in
m. Aur. Lugd.:  <HI REND="ITALIC">«alias eligetur.»</HI>  Usus est igitur Cuj.,
cum pararet Cuj. 1, praeter codicem, ex quo librum
XVI, supplevit, alio codice; qui non dubito quin fuerit
cod. 11. Vid. C. Th. Praefationem. c. 43 h. t., c. 62
 <COL N="0314D"></COL> de Haereticis  <CITN>(XVI, 5)</CITN> , not.  <HI REND="ITALIC">b.</HI>  Recte Go. tuetur  <HI REND="ITALIC">allegetur.</HI></NOTE> , cui nulla ex municipibus prosapia
fuerit, neque ea est opulentia facultatum, quae publicas
functiones facillime queat <NOTE N="g" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0314" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0314D"></COL> g 4  <HI REND="ITALIC">publica—quae ad.</HI>  Inde a vv.  <HI REND="ITALIC">publicas functiones</HI> 
nonnulla discerni possunt in cod. 11.</NOTE>  tolerare; ita ut, si inter
 <COL N="0314B"></COL> civitatem et clericos <NOTE N="h" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0314" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0314D"></COL> h 11  <HI REND="ITALIC">cleros.</HI></NOTE>  super alicujus nomine dubitetur,
si eum aequitas <NOTE N="i" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0314" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0314D"></COL> i Fol. 397 <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0314" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0314C"></COL> a Aur. Lugd. add.  <HI REND="ITALIC">quia jubet lex puniri nefarios.</HI> 
ex Aeg. summa.</NOTE>  cod. 4. 11  <HI REND="ITALIC">equitas aut.</HI></NOTE>  ad publica trahat obsequia, et progenie
municeps vel patrimonio idoneus dignoscetur <NOTE N="j" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0314" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0314D"></COL> j 4  <HI REND="ITALIC">dinoscetus,</HI>  corr. rubro col.  <HI REND="ITALIC">dinoscetur.</HI></NOTE> ,
exemptus clericis civitati tradatur. Opulentos enim
saeculi subire necessitates oportet, pauperes ecclesiarum
divitiis sustentari.  <HI REND="ITALIC">PP. Kal. Jun. Constantino A.</HI> 
VII,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et Constante</HI> <NOTE N="k" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0314" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0314D"></COL> k Be. requirit  <HI REND="ITALIC">Constantio.</HI>  Aur. Lugd.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cons.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">C. Coss.</HI>  (326).</P></DIV2> <DIV2 COM="0314" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0314">DE CURSU PUBLICO.</HEAD> <P COM="0314"><HI REND="ITALIC">Imp. Constantinus A Menandro</HI> <NOTE N="l" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0314" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0314D"></COL> l Codex Lugd.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Id. A. Menandro Certis,</HI>  etc. Deest
igitur dignitas Menandri. Om. ea etiam in omnibus
C. Th. legibus ad Menandrum datis. Vid. C. Th. IV,
12, 2 et 3, infra XI, 27, 2 et XV, 1, 2, quare inter
viros doctos de dignitate Menandri disceptatur. Vid.
C. Th. IV, 12, 2, not.  <HI REND="ITALIC">a.</HI></NOTE> . Certis nuntiis compertum
est, quod plures veluti sibi ac necessitatibus
propriis petitas angarias <NOTE N="m" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0314" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0314D"></COL> m Go.—Ri*.  <HI REND="ITALIC">petitas, angarias,</HI>  male.</NOTE>  taxato pretio distrahunt.
Quamvis itaque raro posthac et non nisi merentibus
evectiones praebendae sint, omnes tamen, qui ubique
sunt cursus publici observatione destricti <NOTE N="n" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0314" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0314D"></COL> n Reinesius cj.  <HI REND="ITALIC">districti.</HI></NOTE> , inquirant,
si quis in hoc genere criminis possit intercipi,
 <COL N="0314C"></COL> ut emptor et venditor in insulam relegetur; illis
etiam <NOTE N="o" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0314" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0314D"></COL> o Hic incipit pag. secunda folii XCII, codicis Lugd.</NOTE>  qui observare jussi sunt, pro dissimulatione
vel negligentia idem supplicium luituris <NOTE N="p" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0314" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0314D"></COL> p Codex  <HI REND="ITALIC">luiturius,</HI>  mendose.</NOTE> , § 1. Non
 <COL N="0315A"></COL> improbum tamen est, si is, qui angarialem habet copiam,
ad tutelam vitae <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0315" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0315B"></COL> a Go. cj.  <HI REND="ITALIC">viae,</HI>  prob. Bondam in Animad. crit. ad
loca quaedam i. civ. depravata  <CITN>(Oelrichs, Thes. nov.
 <COL N="0315C"></COL> Dissertt. jurid. Vol. II, T. II, p. 221)</CITN> . Speciosa est
Go. cj., sed nescio an recipienda.</NOTE>  vel laborem adeundum <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0315" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0315C"></COL> b Go. annotat: «Forte  <HI REND="ITALIC">adimendum:</HI>  Sed nil temere
muto.» Bondam l. c. cj.  <HI REND="ITALIC">obeundum.</HI>  Nihil mutandum
est.</NOTE>  itineris
pro solatio sibi quemdam sociaverit. Namque
hoc factum meretur veniam, nec latere poterit explorantes <NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0315" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0315C"></COL> c Codex  <HI REND="ITALIC">explorante,</HI>  sed appon.  <HI REND="ITALIC">s.</HI>  supra  <HI REND="ITALIC">e.</HI></NOTE> ;
illud poena superius dicta plectendum
est. Super qua re proconsules, rectores provinciarum
 <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0315" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0315C"></COL> d Go. annotat: «Ita locus hic interpungendus.
Nam error est viri docti qui  <HI REND="ITALIC">Provinciarum Praefectos,</HI> 
pro Rectoribus hic somniat: Imo  <HI REND="ITALIC">Praefecti vehiculorum</HI> 
hic alii sunt.»</NOTE>  praefectos vehiculorum atque omnes qui cursui
publico praesunt, admoneri conveniet.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dat.</HI>  X.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Kal. Jul. Constantino</HI> <NOTE N="e" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0315" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0315C"></COL> e Reinesius corr.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Constantio.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">A.</HI>  VII  <HI REND="ITALIC">et Constantio C. Coss.</HI> 
(326).</P></DIV2> <DIV2 COM="0315" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0315">DE OPERIBUS PUBLICIS.</HEAD> <P COM="0315"><HI REND="ITALIC">Imp. Constantinus. a Secundo Pf. P.</HI>  Provinciarum
judices commoneri praecipimus, ut nihil se novi operis
ordinari <NOTE N="f" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0315" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0315C"></COL> f Go. Be. corr.  <HI REND="ITALIC">ordinare,</HI>  recte. Fortasse pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">se</HI> 
